# Job outputs are kept in-tree because the study's results live with its plan, but the bulk
# artefacts must not be: the dumped cost tensor is ~923 MB and the checkpoints are incidental
# (the dump/timing jobs train only far enough to reach the step they measure).
*.pt
checkpoints/
__pycache__/

# Kept: the small files that ARE the results, ~75 kB in total. Each one costs a B200
# allocation to regenerate, so they are cheaper to store than to re-measure.
#
# The re-inclusions below are load-bearing, not decorative: the repo root ignores *.json and
# *.npz globally (.gitignore:9 and :123), which silently swallowed every one of these until
# 2026-08-28. A negation in a deeper .gitignore takes precedence, which is why they work here.
# Do not "tidy" them away -- config.yaml and metadata.yaml would be committed for each run
# while the numbers those runs produced would not be.
#
#   phase0_matcher_timing.json  MatcherTimer's per-bucket summary: the step's time split into
#                               prep / dtoh / solve / device / other, with each bucket's share
#                               of the step. Phase 0's headline -- that the prize is the solve
#                               and not the 921.6 MB device-to-host copy -- is read off these.
#   phase0_matcher_timing.npz   the per-step arrays behind that summary (one value per measured
#                               step, per bucket). Needed for anything the median hides: the
#                               host solve's variance collapsing from 76% to 3.7% relative std
#                               at batch 2048 is only visible here.
#   phase1_logs/*/*.json        the manifest for the dumped cost tensor -- its shape, the crop
#                               it was taken at, and the run it came from. The .pt it describes
#                               is ignored above, so without this the tensor is unidentifiable.
!phase0_logs/*/phase0_matcher_timing.json
!phase0_logs/*/phase0_matcher_timing.npz
!phase1_logs/*/*.json
